await edit('CLAUDE.md', "- `MusicEstimator::ifb_music_spectrum()` — wideband variant; bin frequencies use the estimator's `sample_rate`, so tones above Nyquist cannot be recovered", "- `MusicEstimator::ifb_music_spectrum()` — wideband variant; bin frequencies use the estimator's `sample_rate`, so tones above Nyquist cannot be recovered\n- `select_bins_by_energy()` — picks the IFB bins within N dB of the strongest; with `bins = None` noise-only bins dominate the geometric mean");
await $`git add -A src tests CLAUDE.md`;
await commit(`Add select_bins_by_energy for IFB-MUSIC

IFB-MUSIC weights every bin equally, so with bins = None the noise-only bins
dominate the geometric mean (single recordings off by up to ~130°). The new
helper keeps bins whose cross-spectral power is within threshold_db of the
strongest bin; its result goes into the existing bins argument.

With a 20 dB threshold, every recording below Nyquist is exact at nfft 160
(tones on bins). Three-tone composites are within 2.0° at nfft 160 and 1024;
at 1024 the tones fall between bins and leakage bins are steered at their own
frequency, which is documented on the function.`);
await $`git log --oneline -1`.text()

